+## Built State (F026, 2026-09-25)
+
+What exists on disk at the close of F026, built in five rounds of its first session on
+`feature/f026-task-edit-runtime`, cut from `main` at `90555849`. Every DECISION named lives in
+`.agent/decisions.md`; every round's verdict in `.agent/live_review.md` or, once rotated, its
+archive.
+
+**T001 — the state gate and the versioned apply.** `packages/orchestration/task_edit_runtime.py`
+edits one task of an approved plan while no run holds the job's record, and the edit IS the plan
+editor's own `plan_edit_task`: `apply_edit` and `revalidate` refuse exactly what they refuse before
+approval, one entry joins the same `_edits` log, so `replay_edits` still reconstructs the plan, and
+the plan's `_version` rises. The gate `runtime_edit_state` admits three states and no other —
+`waiting` (a pending task not paused), `paused` (a pending task with a pause file, or in a paused
+job) and `failed` (a task `failed` or `blocked`) — and refuses a running or terminal job, an open or
+rejected approval, and every other task status, each refusal naming the state. The task entry is
+updated in place and keeps its id, its runs and its pause files; `TaskEntry.spec_version` rises by
+one and is the conflict check; the prior spec is archived create-only at
+`task_specs/<planned id>.v<n>.json` in the evidence export before the record is written; the
+approval's hash follows the edit; and a failed task returns to `pending` in the same write together
+with every later task its block skipped (DECISION F026 D1).
+
+**T002 — the channel, the CLI and the trace proof.** `job.edit-task` is a catalog command, a CLI
+verb in `apps/cli/commands/job_plan_cmd.py` that takes a task by its id in the job or in the plan
+and a required `--spec-version`, and a clause of the write door answered by `task_edit_refusal`;
+`job plan-show` prints each task's spec version and status (DECISION F026 D2).
+`TestTracePreservesTheEdit` in `tests/orchestration/test_task_edit_runtime.py` fails a planned
+task under the fake provider, edits it, relaunches, and reads the new run's prompt trace and its
+evidence-export copy: the edited text is there and the old is not. `run_job` now clears a stale job
+error when a relaunch starts running (R-1059).
+
+**T003 — the page and the end-to-end.** The dashboard's `task_specs` section carries each plan
+task's spec, version chain and runtime editability; an edited task shows a `v<n>` chip beside its
+graph node and in the detail popover; the popover's Versions list opens the fields each version
+changed (DECISION F026 D3). The popover offers an "Edit task" form only for a task the dashboard
+marks editable, sent through `apps/ui/src/api/taskEditSend.ts` with only the changed fields, and it
+scrolls within the window (DECISION F026 D4). `tests/ui_server/test_task_edit_e2e_live.py` fails a
+planned job through `python3 -m apps.cli.main job run`, edits it through a live server's door,
+relaunches it through the CLI, and reads the edit in the new trace and two `task_run_started`
+frames for the task in the live server's `events-since`, the run fan the graph draws.
+
+**Acceptance, by the test that proves it.** The editable-state matrix and its named refusals:
+`TestStateGateTaskStatusMatrix`, `TestStateGateJobStateMatrix`, `TestStateGateApproval` and
+`TestRefusalsWriteNothing` in `tests/orchestration/test_task_edit_runtime.py`, the CLI's classes in
+`tests/cli/test_job_plan_cmd.py` and the door's in `tests/ui_server/test_command_dispatch.py`. The
+version chain complete, renderable and immutable: `TestArchive`, with `.v1.json` byte-identical
+after a second edit, `tests/ui_server/test_dashboard_task_specs.py` and
+`apps/ui/src/api/taskSpecView.test.ts`. The v2 trace grep, and a v1 remnant failing it:
+`TestTracePreservesTheEdit` and the end-to-end, and round 2's mutation m2, which leaves the old
+title in the entry and turns the trace proof red. Revalidation refusals change nothing:
+`test_revalidation_refusal_empty_acceptance` with `_assert_refused`, which compares the record's
+bytes, `task_specs/` and the export directory. An acceptance edit after the DoD was compiled marks
+`dod_resync_pending` in the log entry (R-1062). Each round's mutation proofs are its
+`.agent/authored/f026-r<n>-mutations.py`.
+
+**Modules and lists (closure precondition 7).** F026 added `packages/orchestration/task_edit_runtime.py`
+and its line `packages.orchestration.task_edit_runtime` in
+`tests/orchestration/import_reachability_allowlist.txt`; the `ALLOWED_UNWIRED` entry round 1 gave it
+in `tests/test_no_orphan_modules.py` was removed when round 2 wired it, and nothing joined
+`RESERVED_NAMESPACES`. Its other new modules are TypeScript under `apps/ui/src/`:
+`api/taskSpecView.ts`, `api/taskEditSend.ts`, `components/detail/TaskVersionList.tsx` and
+`components/detail/TaskEditForm.tsx`.
+
+**Beyond the code.** Three rows of `docs/ui/design_reference/assumption_log.md` record the chip,
+the Versions list and the edit form, none of which the design reference drew. The secret detector
+`find_forbidden_surface_tokens` now reads an `sk-` key only at a token start, because it read this
+feature's own branch name as a key (R-1060). Clarification immutability, attempt semantics beyond
+the reset and subtree rerun mechanics are untouched.
+
+**Deliberate absences.** No edit of a job built from a job file without a plan, no edit while the
+job runs, and no dependency edit, each named in DECISION F026 D1 as a future feature rather than a
+widening of this one.
+
+**Findings.** F026 registered R-1059 to R-1062. R-1059 and R-1060 are resolved; R-1061 and R-1062
+are repaired by the commits that precede this Built State in the same round, and their resolutions
+are booked by the round after it. The four findings open at its claim, R-1008, R-1055, R-1057 and
+R-1058, are owned by F285 and were neither touched nor re-assigned.
